+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Our services have no common way to refer to a value inside a JSON document. JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) is the
+published standard for this, and later features (e.g. JSON Patch, RFC 6902) are built on it.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`: returns the value the pointer refers to.
+- It throws an error when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer (RFC 6901 §3, §5), or when it does not resolve
+  to a value of the document (RFC 6901 §4).
+- Add an exported `JsonPointerError` class so callers can tell these errors apart from other failures.
+- Add the project's first source and test files; the document is never mutated.
+
+Governing standard: RFC 6901, JSON Pointer, §3 (syntax), §4 (evaluation), §5 (error handling).
+Only the string representation (§5) is covered; the URI fragment representation (§6, `#/a/b`) is out of scope,
+as are creating/setting values, pointer construction/escaping helpers, and JSON Patch.
+
+Nothing is **BREAKING**: there is no existing API.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-pointer`: evaluating an RFC 6901 JSON Pointer string against a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New: `src/index.ts`, tests under `test/`. No dependency or `package.json` change.
+- New public API for importing projects: `resolvePointer`, `JsonPointerError`.
